target/
build/
# Personal data and the register never enter git: history cannot be
# erased, which would make DPDP erasure rights unhonourable.
# `people/*` rather than `people/`: git does not descend into an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so a negation inside one never applies. Ignoring the contents
# instead is what lets the template through.
people/*
store/

# The shape of a record is not data, and a fresh clone needs it: `docket new`
# copies it and twenty tests read it. Excluding the whole directory left a
# checkout that could not open a record.
#
# ONE NEGATION PER TEMPLATE, not a glob. `!people/_TEMPLATE*.yaml` would also
# admit anything a person happened to name that way, and this directory is the
# one place in the repository where a false negative is personal data in git
# history. Adding a class template means adding a line here -- deliberately.
!people/_TEMPLATE.yaml
!people/_TEMPLATE-officer.yaml

# macOS Finder metadata. Untracked noise that a durability-checkpoint commit would
# otherwise sweep into history.
.DS_Store
